HST Office: the notebookbar's UI configuration listener takes the SolarMutex.

ChangedUIEventListener refilled the quick access toolbar (the shortcuts toolbox) and laid out the tab row
from whatever thread changed the module's UI configuration. A UNO client (a macro, an extension, a test
over the remote bridge) changing it from its own thread raced the main loop and crashed in
TabControl::ImplGetItemSize -> OutputDevice::GetCtrlTextWidth (seen on Linux, 14/11/2026). The listener now
holds the SolarMutex and skips a disposed tab control.

--- a/sfx2/source/notebookbar/NotebookbarTabControl.cxx
+++ b/sfx2/source/notebookbar/NotebookbarTabControl.cxx
@@ -391,6 +391,11 @@
     {
         if( rEvent.ResourceURL == TOOLBAR_STR )
         {
+            // HST Office: a UNO client may change the module's UI configuration from its own thread; the
+            // toolbox refill and the tab row layout need the SolarMutex (else they race the main loop)
+            SolarMutexGuard aGuard;
+            if (!m_pParent || m_pParent->isDisposed())
+                return;
             m_pParent->m_bInvalidate = true;
             m_pParent->StateChanged(StateChangedType::UpdateMode);
         }
